CLAUDE CODE RULES - Sounduk API FastAPI Project

=== ENTRY POINT ===
⭐ ALWAYS start by reading context/index.md
This is your map to the entire project documentation and structure.

=== CORE PRINCIPLES ===

1. ARCHITECTURE COMPLIANCE
   - Follow guidelines in context/backend_logic.md
   - All handlers must be async (async def)
   - Use FastAPI Dependency Injection for get_db()
   - Validate with Pydantic v2 (schemas.py)
   - Keep business logic in separate utility files (auth_utils, s3_utils, etc)

2. DATABASE OPERATIONS
   - Refer to context/db_schema.md for tables and relationships
   - Never assume column names - check models.py
   - All ORM queries use SQLAlchemy 2.0 syntax (Mapped, mapped_column)
   - Currently using SQLite with Base.metadata.create_all()
   - TODO: Plan Alembic migration when upgrading

3. API ENDPOINTS
   - Check context/system_map.md for all existing endpoints
   - Every new endpoint must be added to system_map.md (table)
   - Every new endpoint must be documented in task_log.md
   - Follow existing patterns in api/*.py files

4. SECURITY RULES
   - All protected routes need get_current_user() dependency
   - JWT tokens created in auth_utils.py
   - Password hashing: argon2 via passlib
   - Rate limiting exists for registration (3 per IP per 24h)
   - CORS currently open for dev (KI-001: needs restriction for prod)

5. FILE OPERATIONS & INTEGRATIONS
   - S3 storage: use s3_utils.py functions
   - Database backups: handled by db_backup.py (periodic, hourly)
   - Payments: YooKassa API via yookassa SDK
   - Email: SMTP configuration in .env (send_verification_email, etc)

=== WORKFLOW FOR NEW FEATURES ===

When adding a new endpoint:
  1. Read context/backend_logic.md (patterns)
  2. Read context/system_map.md (see similar endpoint)
  3. Create async function in api/*.py
  4. Add Pydantic schema to schemas.py (if input/output needed)
  5. Add row to system_map.md endpoints table
  6. Add entry to task_log.md
  7. Test with ./context/scripts/test_coverage.sh
  8. Commit with: git commit -m "feat: Add endpoint /api/..."

When modifying database:
  1. Update models.py (SQLAlchemy model)
  2. Update schemas.py (Pydantic response)
  3. NOTE: No Alembic yet - changes auto-created on restart (dev only)
  4. TODO: Migrate to Alembic for production

=== HELPFUL SCRIPTS ===

- ./context/scripts/run_dev.sh         → Start dev server (port 8000)
- ./context/scripts/test_coverage.sh   → Run pytest with coverage report
- ./context/scripts/full_migrate.sh    → Placeholder for Alembic (when added)

=== FILE LOCATIONS QUICK REFERENCE ===

Core Files:
  main.py                    → Entry point, FastAPI app config, lifespan
  database.py                → SQLAlchemy engine, SessionLocal, get_db()
  models.py                  → ORM models (User, Track, Album, Payment)
  schemas.py                 → Pydantic validation (DTO)

Utilities:
  auth_utils.py              → JWT, password hashing
  email_utils.py             → Email sending (verify, reset)
  s3_utils.py                → S3 file operations
  db_backup.py               → Periodic S3 database backups

API Routes:
  api/auth.py                → /api/auth/* (register, login, verify)
  api/tracks.py              → /api/tracks/* (upload, stream, cover)
  api/albums.py              → /api/albums/* (create, update, tracks)
  api/users.py               → /api/users/* (profile, storage info)
  api/payments.py            → /api/payments/* (YooKassa)
  api/admin.py               → /api/admin/* (users management)

Context Docs (THIS PROJECT'S KNOWLEDGE BASE):
  context/index.md           → START HERE (overview & quick links)
  context/backend_logic.md   → Coding style, architecture decisions
  context/db_schema.md       → Database structure & relationships
  context/system_map.md      → All endpoints, middleware, services map
  context/task_log.md        → Change history and current work status

=== CRITICAL CONFIGURATION ===

Environment Variables (in .env):
  - SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASSWORD (email)
  - AWS_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_SECRET_KEY (S3)
  - YOOKASSA_SHOP_ID, YOOKASSA_API_KEY (payments)
  - DATABASE_URL (currently sqlite, auto-configured)

Known Issues (context/task_log.md):
  KI-001: CORS open for all origins (need to restrict for prod)
  KI-002: No Alembic migrations (using create_all)
  KI-003: No Docker (needed for deployment)

=== VERSION & DEPENDENCIES ===

Python: 3.9+
FastAPI: 0.115.0
SQLAlchemy: 2.0.36
Pydantic: 2.9.2+
Uvicorn: 0.32.0 (ASGI server)

=== GIT COMMIT CONVENTION ===

Format: git commit -m "type: description"

Types:
  - feat: New feature (endpoint, integration)
  - fix: Bug fix
  - refactor: Code reorganization (no behavior change)
  - test: Test additions/fixes
  - docs: Documentation (not code changes)
  - chore: Dependencies, config

Example:
  git commit -m "feat: Add playlist support to albums endpoint"

=== EVERY TIME YOU CREATE ENDPOINT OR SERVICE ===

✅ Update context/system_map.md (add to endpoints table)
✅ Update context/task_log.md (add history entry)
✅ Test with test_coverage.sh
✅ Follow async/Pydantic patterns from context/backend_logic.md
✅ Commit with proper convention

=== BEFORE CLOSING SESSION ===

If you made changes:
  1. Run ./context/scripts/test_coverage.sh to verify
  2. Update context/task_log.md if work status changed
  3. Check that context/system_map.md is up-to-date
  4. Commit with "git commit -m" using convention above

=== FOR FUTURE CLAUDE SESSIONS ===

Always start with: context/index.md (your north star)
Then check: context/system_map.md (what exists now)
Then refer to: context/backend_logic.md (how to implement)

